handoff

Based on handoff 0.1.0, part of the "benai-mods" Claude Code mods collection by
Ben AI (https://www.benai.co). Redistributed in joel/skill-marketplace with the
author's permission.

Changes from 0.1.0 (in 0.2.0):
- The ~/.claude/mods/switches.json switches and the .open-handoff request file
  (from benai's `mods` pane) are gone. The mod is turned off with
  `/plugin disable handoff`. Two userConfig fields, shown in /config, replace
  them: offer auto|off and offer_at (tokens, default 250000).
- Hide on the offer applies to the current chat only.
- The home directory is read from HOME ($.env.get).
- Copy uses Claude Code's clipboard ($.ui.copy) instead of pbcopy.
- Start new chat: in Zellij it opens a pane beside the chat running claude
  on the handoff; in a plain terminal it copies the handoff and shows the
  command to run; the desktop app keeps its claude:// link. The Claude Pet
  path is gone.
- Open file uses `zellij edit --floating` inside Zellij.
- Tests were updated to match the changes above.
In 0.3.0:
- Start new chat and Open file go through the multiplexer plugin's $.mux (a
  dependency) instead of running zellij itself; with no multiplexer, Open
  file uses open on a Mac and xdg-open elsewhere.

Everything else is the upstream code.
